{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/448161-aeon-trinity-timeline","id":448161,"title":"Aeon Trinity Timeline?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-18T13:28:38-07:00","id":448161,"title":"Aeon Trinity Timeline?","content":"Do we have any idea how long before the new Trinity universe games are released? In the release schedule, it shows as on the horizon, and at 2/7. Considering that we're two years in or so, that would extrapolate to 2020 release date - is that a reasonable interpretation?<br /> <br /> I am very excited about seeing how they bring the timeline up to date, as well as clean up and clarify some more challenging rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3372-schreier","name":"schreier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T13:51:42-07:00","id":448211,"title":"","content":"Well, they have already said that they will be updating it to the near future. They also plan on having more than the original three timelines from the old gaming line. They also have been working on a new system called Sardonyx (see the thread about that for the reactions to the name located in this forum) that will also be used by Scion. <br /> The thing that I am waiting to sink my teeth into is the Sardonyx system itself. I want those meat and potatoes to see how they will revamp the most beloved of all their gaming lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T13:53:00-07:00","id":448213,"title":"","content":"2/7 is the stage of production they're at, not years taken/years expected.<br /> <br /> The major holdup so far has been working on the new system, codenamed Sardonyx. Fingers crossed it should be sorted out this year, as it's now in development.<br /> <br /> If that's the case, at best I'd project Q4 2015, if not 2016.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T14:32:09-07:00","id":448283,"title":"","content":"I knew that 2/7 was the status, not the time - but just figured that it correlated nicely with the 2 years into the project. I did not realize the hold-up in regards to the system, so that clearly explains the delays. If we're talking 9-12 months - that is exciting. I know that the original line took only 11 months or so from inception to release, so it would make sense, especially with the majority of the background set.<br /> <br /> I really loved the biotech, so I can't wait to see the updates and clarifications. And the new system sounds very flexible, so I can understand the need to be deliberate and test extensively.<br /> <br /> I've read a lot of the threads here, and on rpgpost, so I'm sure that the developers have gotten a ton of feedback already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3372-schreier","name":"schreier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T14:39:03-07:00","id":448288,"title":"","content":"I suspect we're getting much closer to the Open Dev of the core system, but in terms of seeing Aeon in our hands? That's not something they're estimating yet. In truth, no-one knows. We do know that first it'll be the Aeon setting book (and a core rules book around the same time). Then sometime after that you'll see Aberrant, Adventure! and other settings built off the core. There's even less information about these and the order of release for these (betting on Aberrant, then Adventure! then 'others').<br /> <br /> Keep an eye on the Monday meeting notes on this site for (infrequent right now) updates. Also, we've got a regularly updated collaborative document listing what we know (with sources linked) <a href=\"https://plus.google.com/u/0/communities/114014290116365242157\" target=\"_blank\">over here</a>. See right side panel for 'What we know so far'. That doesn't contain more timescale stuff outside what you've seen in this thread, but does contain a bunch of pages of collected notes and comments about the reboot from all over the place, if that's your kinda thing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T18:36:06-07:00","id":448591,"title":"","content":"Thanks CHILL! Looks great ... it's very exciting that the Beta is coming up. I'm assuming they have more than enough volunteers to proof everything, but if there is any way to help, I'd be very interested. I am very happy that they're designing the system to scale and allow effective crossover. I do like the &quot;World of Brightness&quot; idea as well. I find my characters, even vampires in nWoD, gravitating towards the &quot;good side&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3372-schreier","name":"schreier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T19:08:04-07:00","id":448635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schreier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/448161-aeon-trinity-timeline?p=448591#post448591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks CHILL! Looks great ... it's very exciting that the Beta is coming up. I'm assuming they have more than enough volunteers to proof everything, but if there is any way to help, I'd be very interested. I am very happy that they're designing the system to scale and allow effective crossover. I do like the &quot;World of Brightness&quot; idea as well. I find my characters, even vampires in nWoD, gravitating towards the &quot;good side&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No problem. There's been suggestions by various people involved with the reboot that there will be an Open Development process on the core book / rules. That should mean anyone who wants to can download the info, and can get to test / proof etc for a while. Unless they change their mind of course (anything's possible).<br /> <br /> I'll give the 'world of brightness' naming / approach a miss as I like shades of gray, but thats a different conversation and one I'm sure i've mentioned in other topics here enough to beat the subject to death, lol <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":232,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","user":"CHILL","date":". 03-18-2015, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T19:37:15-07:00","id":448662,"title":"","content":"Definitely not &quot;beating the dead horse&quot; on the brightness/darkness topic ... but gray is definitely the reality in both cases. Like I said, I found myself gravitating towards positive in the world of darkness, just like some of the aeon/adventure/aberrant characters could go towards the dark.<br /> <br /> The whole Upeo/Ogrotek/Legions clash, the Doyen betraying the Quantakinetics, etc ... there was gray in the old world. Even if Aeon is the good guys, there are gray/medium guys there, even dark ones. <br /> <br /> I'm just excited to see some of the biotech again. I loved the Scarab/Locust/bioVARGs/psi gauntlets, etc ... that really differentiated the game I thought, gave it a different feel than all of the other space opera/sci fi games. 40k has the Tyranid with biotech - but it was one alien race, not in use by humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3372-schreier","name":"schreier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T22:42:21-07:00","id":448871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schreier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/448161-aeon-trinity-timeline#post448161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we have any idea how long before the new Trinity universe games are released? In the release schedule, it shows as on the horizon, and at 2/7. Considering that we're two years in or so, that would extrapolate to 2020 release date - is that a reasonable interpretation?<br /> <br /> I am very excited about seeing how they bring the timeline up to date, as well as clean up and clarify some more challenging rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you read the Monday Meeting Note blog posts, you'll see the Sardonyx System listed there. That's our bottleneck; we can't move forward until that system's done. First draft of the completed system was reportedly sent in last night, so we're getting there. Once Rose has approved it and sends it to the rest of us, and we've had time to poke at it internally for a bit, it'll probably start getting posted publicly for comment. And then we can finish writing these books.<br /> <br /> Depending on how smoothly the process goes, we could see books as early as this year. Trinity Continuum + Aeon first, then Aberrant, then Adventure!. Those will always be the three tentpoles -- the setting is called the <i>Trinity</i>, after all. Additional minor game lines might wait until the end, or they might be released in between, depending on how our workflow goes. Some of them might only be ~50 page settings like Victorian Lost or Mage Noir for the WoD. Others might have enough going on that they require a rulebook closer to full-size.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T23:12:03-07:00","id":448880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/448161-aeon-trinity-timeline?p=448871#post448871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you read the Monday Meeting Note blog posts, you'll see the Sardonyx System listed there. That's our bottleneck; we can't move forward until that system's done. First draft of the completed system was reportedly sent in last night, so we're getting there. Once Rose has approved it and sends it to the rest of us, and we've had time to poke at it internally for a bit, it'll probably start getting posted publicly for comment. And then we can finish writing these books.</div> </div> </div> </div>The anticipation is taking my breath away, but thanks so much for the update here Ian (i assume we're welcome to call you by your first name).<br /> -gibbers excitedly to self on way out-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T11:13:58-07:00","id":449485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First draft of the completed system was reportedly sent in last night, so we're getting there. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'll confirm that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T07:24:36-07:00","id":450416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/448161-aeon-trinity-timeline?p=448871#post448871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you read the Monday Meeting Note blog posts, you'll see the Sardonyx System listed there. That's our bottleneck; we can't move forward until that system's done. First draft of the completed system was reportedly sent in last night, so we're getting there. Once Rose has approved it and sends it to the rest of us, and we've had time to poke at it internally for a bit, it'll probably start getting posted publicly for comment. And then we can finish writing these books.<br /> <br /> Depending on how smoothly the process goes, we could see books as early as this year. Trinity Continuum + Aeon first, then Aberrant, then Adventure!. Those will always be the three tentpoles -- the setting is called the <i>Trinity</i>, after all. Additional minor game lines might wait until the end, or they might be released in between, depending on how our workflow goes. Some of them might only be ~50 page settings like Victorian Lost or Mage Noir for the WoD. Others might have enough going on that they require a rulebook closer to full-size.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is all great news, and much more promising than I had originally feared! I can't wait to see the new system, and then start hearing aeon specific bits ... from what I've seen, it's a reboot but I was wondering if you could elaborate on that at all? Still psions, same orders, qin, chromatics, biotech, etc ...with tweaks or will it be like owod vs nwod with big changes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3372-schreier","name":"schreier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T22:48:51-07:00","id":451322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schreier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/448161-aeon-trinity-timeline?p=450416#post450416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is all great news, and much more promising than I had originally feared! I can't wait to see the new system, and then start hearing aeon specific bits ... from what I've seen, it's a reboot but I was wondering if you could elaborate on that at all? Still psions, same orders, qin, chromatics, biotech, etc ...with tweaks or will it be like owod vs nwod with big changes?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've discussed a fair bit of our plans here in this forum. CHILL has a document where he's compiled a lot of the stuff John and I have said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T22:54:14-07:00","id":451325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/448161-aeon-trinity-timeline?p=448288#post448288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, we've got a regularly updated collaborative document listing what we know (with sources linked) <a href=\"https://plus.google.com/u/0/communities/114014290116365242157\" target=\"_blank\">over here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just for ease of reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T12:58:03-07:00","id":451957,"title":"","content":"Thank you both! I had read that in its entirety, but I missed this one line that answered all of my questions:<br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">All the old allegiances will still be there, plus some more wherever we can cram them in (like those from the TC core). The allegiances may not be exactly the same as before, though. To invent an example, maybe Orgotek is a university rather than a megacorp, but their focus is still on biotech innovations. A shift from before, but not a dramatic 180 or removing them entirely.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Does this mean we're keeping the same aptitudes? The other posts, about the Neptune humanitarians, the transhumanist thinkers, Caribbean freedom fighters, the Theseus and Minoans, and 9 -- are those Aeon-related or in the main &quot;modern day&quot; book?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3372-schreier","name":"schreier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T07:21:20-07:00","id":452632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schreier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/448161-aeon-trinity-timeline?p=451957#post451957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this mean we're keeping the same aptitudes? The other posts, about the Neptune humanitarians, the transhumanist thinkers, Caribbean freedom fighters, the Theseus and Minoans, and 9 -- are those Aeon-related or in the main &quot;modern day&quot; book?</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't know yet and the devs / writers are being careful not to give too much concrete information yet as the system mechanics are still being worked on. There will be some similarities, but also some changes. Expect change, I think <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T11:24:20-07:00","id":452918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schreier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/448161-aeon-trinity-timeline?p=451957#post451957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this mean we're keeping the same aptitudes? The other posts, about the Neptune humanitarians, the transhumanist thinkers, Caribbean freedom fighters, the Theseus and Minoans, and 9 -- are those Aeon-related or in the main &quot;modern day&quot; book?</div> </div> </div> </div>9 at least are modern-day (they're tagged as having suffered cutbacks in the Reagan era and may well join up with the Directive when Aberrant rolls around), and from context I'd guess the other groups are too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T12:15:06-07:00","id":452991,"title":"","content":"I could tell they were definitely modern, but not sure if they continued forward (a la Aeon itself) .. my guess is that it's included in the &quot;<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">plus some more wherever we can cram them in (like those from the TC core)&quot; </span></span></span>comment ... basically, whoever they can fit in and that makes sense.<br /> <br /> The two things that I really hope they add/adjust are:<br /> 1. give modes/powers that make the gifted more effective bioVARG/VARG/fighter/starship pilots (and maybe even hackers) - something that maybe lets them interface directly into the device to improve reaction time or put more of themselves into it (maybe be able almost possess or meld with the item - see as if they were it,feel the hits, etc)<br /> <br /> 2. improve the ability for psions to actually use their powers (mode natural merit was one really good example - another could be to make the psi pool larger than the psi rating - like 2x psi, or grows exponentially (2 at 2, 4 at 3, 8 at 4, etc....)<br /> <br /> It sounds like it won't be too much longer til we start seeing some rules trickle out - will be awesome! I'm curious how rolls/systems will be since it specifically isn't the storyteller system but sounds like it will still be trait/skill based with d10s ... I'm dying to see how these &quot;environmental dice&quot; work - scaling will be huge, especially with scions, abberrants, normals and psions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3372-schreier","name":"schreier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T12:25:12-07:00","id":453012,"title":"","content":"At least one of the groups from the TC core appears in some form within Aeon, at least implicitly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T16:41:09-07:00","id":453352,"title":"","content":"Thanks Ian! Can't wait to see it. I really like the sound of the TC core - I've always found a modern day game an easy bridge for new roleplayers ... they can imagine themselves in a world they know. Playing fantasy worlds, historic worlds, and scifi is always a challenge because we all imagine them differently. Having a foundation where we are all working on the same basic understanding can let you focus more on the characters. Will TC core be pre-psi (basically we'll have Adventure in the 20's or whatever, then TC with the same basic power concepts, then Aberrant, then Aeon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3372-schreier","user":"schreier","date":". 03-22-2015, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3372-schreier","name":"schreier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}